{"strongs": "H5271", "word": "נְעוּרִים", "translit": "na.ur", "root": "נעורים", "morph": "H:N-M/F", "pos": "noun [masculine] plural", "gloss": "youth, early life", "definition": "נְעוּרִים noun [masculine] plural youth, early life ; — absolute ׳ נ Isa 54:6 ; Ps 127:4 elsewhere suffix נְעֻרַי 1Sam 12:2 , נְעוּרַי Job 31:18 +, נְעֻרֶיךָ 2Sam 19:8 , נְעוּרֶיךָ Prov 5:18 +, נְעוּרַיִךְ Jer 2:2 +, נְעוּרָ֑יְכִי Ps 103:5 , נְעוּרֵיהֶן Ezek 23:3 , etc.; — youth, early life , especially in phrase ׳ מִנּ from one's youth up Gen 8:21 ( J ), 1Sam 17:33 ; 1Kgs 18:12 ; Jer 3:24 ; Zech 13:5 ; Job 31:18 (extreme youth; || מִבֶּטֶן אִמִּי ); figurative of Babylon Isa 47:12 ; Isa 47:15 , Moab Jer 48:11 , Judah Jer 22:21 compare Ps 71:5 ; Ps 71:17 ; Ps 129:1 ; Ps 129:2 וְעַדעַֿתָּה ׳ מִנּ Gen 46:34 ( J ), 2Sam 19:8 ; Ezek 4:14 וְעַדהַֿיּוֺם הַזֶּה ׳ מִנּ 1Sam 12:2 ; Jer 3:25 as time in or during which Lev 22:13 ( H ), Num 30:4 ; Num 30:17 ( P ), Lam 3:27 ; Ps 144:12 , figurative of Judah and Samaria, personified, Ezek 23:2 ; Ezek 23:8 compare ׳ יְמֵי נ (in figurative of Israel) Hos 2:17 (|| יוֺם עֲלוֺתָהּ מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרָ֑יִם ), Ezek 16:22 ; Ezek 16:43 ; Ezek 16:60 ; Ezek 23:19 other phrase are: ׳ אַלּוּף נ Jer 3:4 friend of my youth , compare Prov 2:17 , ׳ עֲוֺנוֺת נ Job 13:26 , ׳ חַטּאֹות נ Ps 25:7 , ׳ חֶסֶד נ Jer 2:2 , ׳ חֶרְפַּת נ Jer 31:19 , ׳ זִמַּת נ Ezek 23:21 , ׳ שְׁדֵי נ v Ezek 23:21 , ׳ בַּעַל נ Joel 1:8 , and especially ׳ אֵשֶׁת נ Prov 5:18 ; Mal 2:14 ; Mal 2:15 ; Isa 54:6 (figurative); ׳ בְּנֵי נ Ps 127:4 sons of (a man's) youth ; = youthful vigour Ps 103:5 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5280')\">BDB5280</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H5271')\">H5271</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5279')\">BDB5279</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5281')\">BDB5281</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>נְעוּרִים</bdbheb> <b>noun [masculine] plural</b> <highlightword>youth, early life</highlightword>; — absolute <bdbheb>׳</bd